Usage: run [-hV] [--dev] [--proxy-setup] [--validate-enforce] [--watch]
           [-extensions=<extensions>] [--init=<init>] [-l=<logLevel>]
           [--openapi=<openapi>] [-p=<port>] [--persist=<persist>]
           [--proxy-to=<proxyTo>] [--validate-openapi=<validateOpenapi>]
           [-D=<key=value>]...
Start MockServer (default subcommand).
  -D=<key=value>             Set a JVM system property before startup, e.g.
                               -Dmockserver.metricsEnabled=true (repeatable).
                               Equivalent to a JVM -D but accepted after the
                               launcher/jar. Any system property is accepted;
                               use mockserver.* keys for MockServer
                               configuration.
      --dev                  Enable developer-friendly defaults: reduced memory
                               caps (maxLogEntries=1000, maxExpectations=1000)
                               for laptop/test-suite use. Explicit config
                               (system property, env var, or properties file)
                               overrides dev-mode defaults.
      -extensions, --extensions=<extensions>
                             Comma-separated extension class names (each
                               implementing org.mockserver.extension.Extension)
                               to load and start at startup; their JARs must be
                               on the classpath. Equivalent to
                               MOCKSERVER_EXTENSIONS or -Dmockserver.extensions.
  -h, --help                 Show this help message and exit.
      --init=<init>          Initialize expectations from a JSON file path or
                               glob pattern.
  -l, --log-level=<logLevel> Log level: TRACE, DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR, OFF
                               (or Java Logger equivalents).
      --openapi=<openapi>    Initialize expectations from an OpenAPI spec URL
                               or file path.
  -p, --port=<port>          Port(s) to listen on (comma-separated list, e.g.
                               1080,1081). Required unless set via the
                               MOCKSERVER_SERVER_PORT environment variable, the
                               mockserver.serverPort system property, or a
                               properties file.
      --persist=<persist>    Enable expectation persistence and set the file
                               path.
      --proxy-setup          Set MockServer up as a TLS-intercepting proxy:
                               generate a unique private Certificate Authority
                               (instead of the public CA published in the
                               MockServer repository) and print an OS-specific
                               copy-paste setup block (CA path plus HTTPS_PROXY
                               / NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS / SSL_CERT_FILE /
                               REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE exports). Equivalent to
                               MOCKSERVER_PROXY_SETUP=true or -Dmockserver.
                               proxySetup=true.
      --proxy-to=<proxyTo>   Forward unmatched requests to host[:port] (enables
                               port-forwarding mode).
  -V, --version              Print version information and exit.
      --validate-enforce     When combined with --validate-openapi, reject
                               requests that violate the spec (400) and replace
                               non-conformant upstream responses (502). Without
                               this flag, violations are report-only.
      --validate-openapi=<validateOpenapi>
                             Validate forwarded/proxied requests and responses
                               against the given OpenAPI spec (URL, file path,
                               or inline payload). Violations are logged;
                               combine with --validate-enforce to block
                               non-conformant traffic.
      --watch                Watch the initializer/expectations file(s) (from
                               --init / --openapi) and live-reload expectations
                               when they change, without a restart (~5s poll).
                               Equivalent to
                               MOCKSERVER_WATCH_INITIALIZATION_JSON=true or
                               -Dmockserver.watchInitializationJson=true.
